WEBVTT

00:22.981 --> 00:24.858
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:33.093 --> 01:35.846
While you guys were turning
to stone, bleeding from your nose,

01:35.929 --> 01:38.765
and getting engrossed in hunting for food,

01:39.307 --> 01:42.102
I managed to find some patterns
in the shifts of the dungeon.

01:42.185 --> 01:44.604
It's not like I wanted
to be turned to stone.

01:44.688 --> 01:45.814
Hear, hear!

01:45.897 --> 01:48.358
The past three days
have been very productive!

01:48.441 --> 01:49.484
Yeah, whatever.

01:50.193 --> 01:52.612
One path gets blocked
and another one opens up.

01:52.696 --> 01:54.489
It's basically this on repeat.

01:55.532 --> 01:58.869
The number of doors, furniture,
and types of buildings stay the same.

01:58.952 --> 02:01.371
A house never transforms into a graveyard.

02:01.454 --> 02:04.875
The walls move in a clockwise spiral
at regular intervals.

02:05.458 --> 02:08.461
The positions of the stone statues
and the directions they face are fixed.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.380
Based on all that and more…

02:14.342 --> 02:16.178
I remember this street.

02:16.261 --> 02:19.014
That's the house where we ate the Dragon.

02:19.097 --> 02:21.099
Chilchuck, you're a genius!

02:21.183 --> 02:23.101
Well, it's all in a day's work.

02:25.020 --> 02:26.855
But this street…

02:27.355 --> 02:28.899
<i>Exactly.</i>

02:29.482 --> 02:30.984
<i>It's where we lost Falin.</i>

02:31.067 --> 02:33.904
<i>There was a pool of blood
and traces of something being dragged.</i>

02:33.987 --> 02:34.863
<i>It's Falin!</i>

02:34.946 --> 02:37.365
<i>If those two catch sight of it,
they'll get worked up for sure.</i>

02:37.449 --> 02:39.159
<i>How am I going to make them stay calm?</i>

02:39.242 --> 02:40.410
Laios, look!

02:41.912 --> 02:42.787
What is this?

02:42.871 --> 02:45.582
Listen! I get that there's a lot
to be concerned about,

02:45.665 --> 02:48.460
but for now, let's focus
on getting back to the surface and…

02:49.461 --> 02:50.295
Huh?

02:55.133 --> 02:58.678
The Dragon's carcass was here, right?

02:58.762 --> 03:00.889
It's vanished, without a trace.

03:01.890 --> 03:07.062
But this crack in the wall must've been
made when the Red Dragon fell.

03:07.646 --> 03:10.023
But even this crack is being repaired…

03:13.985 --> 03:16.404
The magician's eye will be upon you.

03:18.323 --> 03:20.700
Don't yell like that!

03:20.784 --> 03:22.619
Just now, I saw…

03:25.205 --> 03:27.499
I think it's mana sickness again.

03:27.582 --> 03:28.667
Again?

03:28.750 --> 03:33.129
Ever since I used healing magic,
I sometimes see and hear things.

03:33.213 --> 03:34.506
You hear things?

03:34.589 --> 03:36.508
Are you sure it's mana sickness?

03:36.591 --> 03:37.842
What did you hear?

03:38.635 --> 03:40.762
"The magician's eye will be upon you."

03:40.845 --> 03:42.555
"The magician's eye"?

03:43.890 --> 03:44.766
Could it be…

03:49.354 --> 03:50.647
The sound of wings!

03:50.730 --> 03:52.023
It's that Little Dragon!

03:52.107 --> 03:53.149
We need to hide!

03:53.233 --> 03:54.693
Hide where exactly?

03:54.776 --> 03:56.778
This place is too exposed.

03:56.861 --> 03:58.780
We've got to run, Marcille!

03:58.863 --> 04:00.657
No, I know where to hide.

04:02.117 --> 04:03.618
Inside the wall!

04:06.955 --> 04:08.873
Come on, you two! Hurry!

04:08.957 --> 04:10.166
Is this…

04:10.250 --> 04:12.419
Another one of her spells?

04:27.100 --> 04:31.813
Marcille, what kind of magic was that?

04:35.692 --> 04:36.985
Cleaners?

04:37.068 --> 04:38.403
What?

04:38.486 --> 04:39.904
Dungeon Cleaners.

04:39.988 --> 04:42.073
They're creatures, I think,

04:42.157 --> 04:45.452
that keep the dungeon clean
and fix up any damages.

04:45.535 --> 04:46.369
Exactly.

04:46.453 --> 04:50.081
I figured this wall
wasn't completely set yet.

04:50.582 --> 04:52.459
Up until this point is the original wall,

04:53.084 --> 04:54.753
and from here on are Cleaners.

04:54.836 --> 04:55.962
Even the floor!

04:56.046 --> 04:56.880
Check it out!

04:56.963 --> 04:59.758
Even the wear and tear
and tiny scratches are being recreated.

04:59.841 --> 05:02.135
You can't tell the difference by sight.

05:04.512 --> 05:05.347
Ugh!

05:05.430 --> 05:08.850
There are tiny things
crawling all over the floor!

05:08.933 --> 05:09.851
Gross!

05:10.685 --> 05:12.270
They're all Cleaners.

05:12.771 --> 05:15.607
Any dungeon without them
would fall apart in no time.

05:16.191 --> 05:18.109
They're not monsters and aren't harmful.

05:18.193 --> 05:19.778
They are harmful.

05:19.861 --> 05:23.114
These suckers often nibble on my tent.

05:24.783 --> 05:28.995
<i>They break down anything
they think is in the way.</i>

05:29.579 --> 05:32.874
<i>They must've come to eat the remains
of the Dragon and the explosion.</i>

05:33.458 --> 05:35.585
They show up when the dungeon is damaged,

05:35.668 --> 05:38.630
and their secretion prevents fires
from spreading and further collapses.

05:38.713 --> 05:42.050
Then they start devouring
any scattered rubble.

05:42.133 --> 05:43.384
They're not picky eaters.

05:43.968 --> 05:47.222
Finally, they excrete secretions
to fill in the broken areas

05:47.305 --> 05:49.849
and restore the dungeon
to its former state.

05:50.350 --> 05:53.019
It's similar to how creatures heal.

05:53.103 --> 05:54.521
All things considered,

05:54.604 --> 05:57.607
monsters act like the immune system,
clearing out germs.

05:57.690 --> 05:58.900
Who are you calling germs?

05:58.983 --> 06:01.611
Is that also magic at work?

06:01.694 --> 06:02.904
Pretty cool, huh?

06:02.987 --> 06:04.280
Good grief.

06:04.364 --> 06:06.825
What's next, a magical digestive system?

06:07.325 --> 06:10.495
I wonder what the dungeon
would eat in that case?

06:12.580 --> 06:14.749
<i>Thank goodness the bloodstains are gone.</i>

06:15.250 --> 06:16.459
Hey.

06:16.543 --> 06:18.795
Let's get moving
before the dungeon shifts again.

06:18.878 --> 06:19.754
Right.

06:34.561 --> 06:36.729
Stairs!

06:37.772 --> 06:40.024
Finally, a way out.

06:40.108 --> 06:43.570
Well then, how about
we start preparing that?

06:43.653 --> 06:46.197
Good idea. Let's do that.

06:46.781 --> 06:47.615
That?

06:48.158 --> 06:49.617
Oh, you mean that.

06:57.625 --> 07:00.170
Huh? By that, you meant a meal?

07:00.253 --> 07:02.755
I don't think there are
any Tentacles on this level.

07:02.839 --> 07:04.174
You should've said earlier!

07:04.257 --> 07:05.967
You actually like that outfit, don't you?

07:06.050 --> 07:06.926
I don't!

07:09.596 --> 07:13.600
We've got so many ingredients,
I'm not sure what to make.

07:14.684 --> 07:16.311
Maybe I can try using that.

07:17.020 --> 07:18.354
Cook up some grain.

07:18.438 --> 07:20.440
Is it the stuff from the third floor?

07:21.024 --> 07:24.277
I was saving it
for when we ran out of food.

07:25.153 --> 07:26.946
Chop up some Cockatrice meat,

07:27.030 --> 07:28.823
Dryad fruit,

07:28.907 --> 07:30.450
Mandrake fruit and leaves,

07:31.034 --> 07:33.703
and depetrification herbs,

07:34.287 --> 07:36.206
Season them and sauté.

07:36.956 --> 07:39.709
Spread a layer of cooked grain
inside hollowed-out bricks.

07:40.293 --> 07:42.962
Add the toppings
and heat them, brick and all.

07:43.796 --> 07:44.964
And…

07:45.048 --> 07:46.841
Huh? What's that?

07:46.925 --> 07:48.718
A Cockatrice egg.

07:51.054 --> 07:52.972
I brought one along,

07:53.056 --> 07:55.475
but it's been a bit tricky to use.

07:58.061 --> 08:00.730
Finally, pour on the egg sauce and

08:00.813 --> 08:02.148
it's ready.

08:02.232 --> 08:04.734
STONE-BAKED COCKATRICE
CHICKEN AND EGG WITH SAUCE

08:04.817 --> 08:06.528
Wow, what is this?

08:06.611 --> 08:07.654
It looks delicious!

08:08.321 --> 08:12.492
<i>If I'd stayed petrified,
would they have used me to make this dish?</i>

08:17.747 --> 08:19.374
The scorched grain is nice!

08:19.457 --> 08:22.418
Try digging your spoon into the dish.

08:25.713 --> 08:29.384
I used bricks made from Dungeon Cleaners.

08:29.467 --> 08:31.844
So we can even eat the dish?

08:33.096 --> 08:35.181
Thanks, Senshi!

08:39.936 --> 08:41.020
What does it taste like?

08:41.104 --> 08:43.356
At first, it tastes like dirt.

08:43.898 --> 08:44.941
But as you savor it,

08:45.024 --> 08:48.236
it's like this magical blend
of green caterpillar, iron, and lemon.

08:48.945 --> 08:50.822
You're just comparing it to other things.

08:51.364 --> 08:53.825
There's no other way to describe it.

08:53.908 --> 08:56.744
Are you sure it's safe
to eat magical creatures?

08:56.828 --> 08:59.414
It might make you hear things
and bleed from your nose again.

08:59.497 --> 09:01.624
I wonder what's with those hallucinations.

09:03.376 --> 09:05.753
When we get back to town,
you should really see a doctor

09:05.837 --> 09:06.671
for your head.

09:06.754 --> 09:07.672
A doctor?

09:07.755 --> 09:10.049
Do you think it's some kind of illness?

09:16.764 --> 09:18.182
Is this another hallucination?

09:18.266 --> 09:20.059
Are you guys seeing this?

09:20.935 --> 09:22.687
I-I see it.

09:23.521 --> 09:25.690
I mean, we're…

09:26.316 --> 09:27.900
under attack!

09:32.822 --> 09:34.824
Huh? What on earth?

09:34.907 --> 09:36.451
It's just frog skin.

09:37.910 --> 09:41.080
Looks like these horns
are just decorations on a helmet.

09:41.873 --> 09:42.915
A child?

09:45.668 --> 09:47.962
Some monsters
disguise themselves as humans.

09:48.546 --> 09:52.342
Let's try killing one to see
if they'll reveal their true colors--

09:52.425 --> 09:54.260
Don't, Maizuru.

09:58.306 --> 09:59.390
I know them.

09:59.474 --> 10:00.642
-Shuro!
-Shuro!

10:01.684 --> 10:03.770
Shuro, long time no see!

10:03.853 --> 10:07.523
What a pleasant surprise
to run into you here!

10:08.149 --> 10:09.275
Did you lose weight?

10:16.991 --> 10:18.660
Thanks, Shuro!

10:19.827 --> 10:22.080
Glad to see you're doing well.

10:22.163 --> 10:23.915
Goodness! How forward of him!

10:23.998 --> 10:25.500
Oh, let me introduce you.

10:26.334 --> 10:27.460
This is Senshi.

10:27.543 --> 10:30.922
Senshi, meet Shuro,
our former party member.

10:31.005 --> 10:32.882
Shuro? Who's that?

10:32.965 --> 10:35.051
They probably mean Young Master Toshiro.

10:35.802 --> 10:37.679
Toshuro?

10:40.139 --> 10:42.141
Let's continue
our conversation sitting down.

10:42.642 --> 10:44.227
We were just having a meal.

10:45.019 --> 10:46.688
Would you all like to…

10:47.605 --> 10:50.775
Huh? You've got quite a big group!

10:51.776 --> 10:53.194
Hey, Kabru.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.362
Is that…

10:56.948 --> 10:57.949
Nice to meet you.

10:59.659 --> 11:01.077
You're Laios, aren't you?

11:03.162 --> 11:03.996
Yeah.

11:04.080 --> 11:05.331
Nice to meet you.

11:09.085 --> 11:10.837
How long has it been?

11:12.422 --> 11:13.589
Hey, Kabru.

11:14.090 --> 11:15.425
It's them, right?

11:15.508 --> 11:17.218
The ones who stole our stuff.

11:17.760 --> 11:18.761
What will you do?

11:20.596 --> 11:21.722
Nothing.

11:21.806 --> 11:22.640
Huh?

11:22.723 --> 11:24.851
What did we come all the way here for?

11:29.480 --> 11:31.065
I wanted to meet them.

11:31.566 --> 11:32.400
Huh?

11:33.067 --> 11:35.611
<i>I doubt asking them
about the treasure will help.</i>

11:36.237 --> 11:38.865
<i>He didn't look guilty even when he saw us.</i>

11:39.740 --> 11:42.910
Either he doesn't remember,
or we're mistaken.

11:42.994 --> 11:45.705
Or maybe the treasure itself was a trap.

11:45.788 --> 11:47.373
Or maybe all of them.

11:47.457 --> 11:49.292
Are you saying
we made this trip for nothing?

11:49.375 --> 11:50.501
Don't be hasty.

11:50.585 --> 11:52.170
Give me a bit more time.

11:52.712 --> 11:55.423
Don't you want to find out
how they managed to get here

11:55.506 --> 11:58.843
and what they plan to do in the future?

11:59.510 --> 12:03.598
So, you've been
on this level for a while now?

12:03.681 --> 12:04.557
Yeah.

12:04.640 --> 12:06.809
<i>We kept going around in circles,</i>

12:06.893 --> 12:08.811
<i>and when we got out,
we were back at the entrance.</i>

12:09.312 --> 12:11.564
<i>We got lost a lot too.</i>

12:11.647 --> 12:14.817
But Chilchuck
found patterns in the shifts,

12:14.901 --> 12:17.153
and that's how we finally made it here.

12:17.236 --> 12:18.070
I see.

12:18.738 --> 12:21.073
Anyway, Shuro, you…

12:23.659 --> 12:25.495
You lech!

12:25.578 --> 12:27.205
Are they the connections you mentioned?

12:27.288 --> 12:28.331
Lucky you!

12:30.208 --> 12:31.292
They're just retainers.

12:32.293 --> 12:33.794
They're quite skilled, though.

12:35.129 --> 12:36.923
I'm sorry for leaving the party.

12:37.632 --> 12:40.968
But when I realized Falin
was missing up on the surface,

12:41.552 --> 12:47.058
I thought this was the best way
to get back into the dungeon and find her.

12:48.309 --> 12:49.352
Forgive me.

12:49.435 --> 12:51.354
It's fine. There was no other way.

12:51.938 --> 12:55.566
But I'm surprised you went back
into the dungeon right after that.

12:55.650 --> 12:57.235
Wasn't it a little rash?

12:57.818 --> 13:00.696
What would you have done
if someone got hurt again?

13:02.823 --> 13:04.116
Just so you know,

13:05.076 --> 13:08.371
the four of us
even defeated the Red Dragon!

13:08.454 --> 13:09.372
What?!

13:09.956 --> 13:11.082
The Red Dragon?

13:12.333 --> 13:13.876
A-And what about her?

13:17.505 --> 13:18.381
Shuro!

13:18.464 --> 13:19.298
Young Master!

13:20.007 --> 13:23.427
I beg you, please eat and get some sleep!

13:23.511 --> 13:25.555
At this rate, your body will break down!

13:25.638 --> 13:27.765
You're pushing yourself that hard?

13:27.848 --> 13:30.518
Look at how gaunt he is.
You should've noticed.

13:31.227 --> 13:34.146
You should get food and sleep, you know.

13:34.772 --> 13:37.817
I don't have time for that.

13:37.900 --> 13:41.696
Shuro, eating isn't something
you do when you have time.

13:42.280 --> 13:44.907
It's only after having sleep and food

13:44.991 --> 13:48.119
that creatures can
finally do what they want.

13:49.996 --> 13:51.038
Have something to eat.

13:51.747 --> 13:54.083
While you do, I'll fill you in
on what happened.

13:56.168 --> 13:57.670
Fine.

13:57.753 --> 14:00.923
Can you prepare something, Maizuru?

14:03.884 --> 14:06.596
A meal! Prepare a meal!

14:07.179 --> 14:08.973
Tade, go fetch some water!

14:09.056 --> 14:10.099
On it!

14:10.182 --> 14:13.811
Hien, Benichidori, get ready to cook rice.

14:14.312 --> 14:15.897
Asebi, you…

14:18.149 --> 14:20.318
guard the Young Master.

14:20.401 --> 14:22.737
I don't want anything strange
mixed into the food.

14:22.820 --> 14:25.740
Well then, I'll get the fire going.

14:25.823 --> 14:27.491
You are considerate.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.076
I'll leave it to you, dwarf.

14:31.037 --> 14:32.496
A meal, a meal!

14:32.580 --> 14:34.498
This group is too big.

14:35.082 --> 14:37.752
It's not safe for so many people
to gather in one place.

14:38.461 --> 14:39.921
Let's split up into three.

14:41.672 --> 14:42.757
In that case,

14:43.341 --> 14:45.134
Rin, dwarf,

14:45.676 --> 14:46.594
frog woman!

14:46.677 --> 14:47.511
What?!

14:47.595 --> 14:50.848
Everyone who can use magic,
put up a barrier.

14:51.349 --> 14:54.477
Make sure no monsters disturb
the Young Master while he eats.

14:55.978 --> 14:58.397
Let's work together, young lady.

14:58.481 --> 15:00.232
R-Right.

15:00.983 --> 15:01.984
Okay then,

15:02.068 --> 15:04.111
Shuro, let's step away too.

15:04.695 --> 15:06.530
I'll give you a quick rundown.

15:07.114 --> 15:07.990
I'll help support him.

15:08.074 --> 15:08.908
Thanks.

15:09.867 --> 15:11.285
There's so much to do!

15:11.369 --> 15:15.289
<i>In this case,
who's more dangerous if left alone?</i>

15:15.373 --> 15:18.668
Monsters! Delicious! Awesome!

15:19.251 --> 15:22.004
Monsters! Cook! Eat!

15:22.088 --> 15:23.130
Eat this!

15:23.631 --> 15:24.674
Die.

15:24.757 --> 15:27.426
Senshi, I'm coming with you!

15:40.272 --> 15:43.442
Hey, aren't you overdoing it?

15:43.526 --> 15:44.568
The smoke…

15:45.945 --> 15:48.531
After this meal,
I must make him take a bath.

15:48.614 --> 15:49.573
<i>Here?</i>

15:50.157 --> 15:52.118
Okay, Shuro, sit here.

15:52.201 --> 15:54.537
Never mind that,
just tell me what happened.

15:55.705 --> 15:58.332
After you and Namari left, we--

15:58.416 --> 15:59.667
Just give me the gist.

16:00.668 --> 16:04.839
We defeated the Red Dragon,
retrieved Falin, and revived her.

16:04.922 --> 16:07.466
But on our way back,
we were attacked by the lunatic magician,

16:07.550 --> 16:08.759
and we lost her.

16:09.677 --> 16:12.096
There was nothing more
we could do on our own,

16:12.680 --> 16:15.683
so we decided to head back
to the surface and ask for backup.

16:16.267 --> 16:17.393
But we got lost and…

16:18.436 --> 16:21.313
But I'm glad we
crossed paths with you, Shuro!

16:21.397 --> 16:23.232
Will you help us out?

16:26.569 --> 16:28.320
Um, can I ask something?

16:28.821 --> 16:33.200
The lunatic magician is the one
who created this dungeon, right?

16:34.201 --> 16:36.454
<i>There are rumors and whispers about him,</i>

16:36.537 --> 16:39.123
<i>but no one who's seen him
has ever returned.</i>

16:39.206 --> 16:41.292
How can you be sure it was him?

16:41.792 --> 16:42.877
Huh?

16:42.960 --> 16:45.629
Well, he sounded and acted like it.

16:45.713 --> 16:48.883
And how did you manage to escape?

16:48.966 --> 16:50.342
It was thanks to Marcille…

16:51.552 --> 16:53.888
The mage in our party protected us.

16:53.971 --> 16:55.139
How exactly?

16:55.222 --> 16:56.849
Um…

16:57.892 --> 17:00.478
Magic isn't my area of expertise,
so I'm not sure.

17:01.729 --> 17:02.605
I see.

17:04.857 --> 17:06.609
I have a question too.

17:14.283 --> 17:16.202
Why were you munching on a brick?

17:16.702 --> 17:17.703
Huh?

17:17.787 --> 17:19.413
Oh, it's not what it seems.

17:19.497 --> 17:20.706
That wasn't a brick.

17:20.790 --> 17:23.375
It was part of a wall
made from Dungeon Cleaners.

17:23.959 --> 17:27.379
We left all our food
and money behind, right?

17:27.463 --> 17:32.218
So to get down into the dungeon faster,
we fed on monsters along the way.

17:39.642 --> 17:40.518
That…

17:42.228 --> 17:44.647
is just hilarious!

17:44.730 --> 17:45.564
Huh?

17:45.648 --> 17:47.775
What was the tastiest thing
you've eaten so far?

17:47.858 --> 17:49.026
You want to know?

17:49.110 --> 17:50.277
That's a tough one.

17:50.361 --> 17:52.196
Kelpie, Living Armor…

17:52.279 --> 17:54.281
No, it's got to be the Red Dragon!

17:54.365 --> 17:57.243
You ate the Red Dragon
that ate your sister?

17:57.326 --> 17:58.494
Yeah.

17:58.577 --> 18:01.163
Living Armor, though.
Are there any edible parts?

18:01.247 --> 18:02.790
That's a good question!

18:02.873 --> 18:06.001
Actually, it's a colony of mollusks
wearing a shell and…

18:06.085 --> 18:07.294
Here, check out this sword.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.047
The Cleaners are trying to eat Kensuke!

18:10.131 --> 18:12.049
You just can't be too careful!

18:12.133 --> 18:14.927
By the way, if you're interested
in monster cuisine,

18:15.010 --> 18:16.512
I'd be happy to treat you anytime.

18:16.595 --> 18:18.722
Wow, I'd love that!

18:18.806 --> 18:21.934
<i>Crap. This guy will actually
take me up on it.</i>

18:24.645 --> 18:26.564
So after she…

18:27.231 --> 18:30.401
After Falin was revived,
was she safe the last time you saw her?

18:31.360 --> 18:32.194
Yeah.

18:32.278 --> 18:33.904
Any idea where she might be?

18:34.530 --> 18:37.032
There are plenty of places
to hide on this level,

18:37.116 --> 18:39.201
but most of them are the orcs' base camps.

18:39.285 --> 18:41.912
Oh, you don't have to worry about them.

18:41.996 --> 18:42.872
What?

18:44.915 --> 18:45.958
What did they taste like?

18:46.041 --> 18:47.042
No!

18:47.126 --> 18:50.129
It's a long story,
but we're cooperating with them now.

18:51.172 --> 18:53.382
Cooperating with them?

18:53.465 --> 18:56.594
<i>Has he forgotten that killing them
is our duty as adventurers?</i>

18:57.178 --> 18:59.096
Anyway, about Falin's whereabouts,

18:59.180 --> 19:02.099
she might be somewhere
lower than this level.

19:02.683 --> 19:05.060
She could have been taken there.

19:05.686 --> 19:07.605
Taken? Why?

19:07.688 --> 19:09.273
Um…

19:10.441 --> 19:12.568
<i>Is it safe to tell Shuro?</i>

19:13.569 --> 19:15.988
Would you mind if I talked to him alone?

19:16.071 --> 19:18.115
Sure, I'll step out.

19:26.290 --> 19:27.124
So?

19:33.172 --> 19:37.009
Field ration pellets aren't bad,
but having them every day?

19:37.092 --> 19:40.721
Sometimes, you need something
warm in your belly.

19:40.804 --> 19:41.889
I agree.

19:41.972 --> 19:46.060
A meal should be more than
about filling the stomach.

19:46.143 --> 19:48.103
I see you have sense, dwarf.

19:48.604 --> 19:51.398
The Young Master
was often sick as a child.

19:51.482 --> 19:55.527
He also had a small appetite,
which worried everyone.

19:55.611 --> 20:00.824
<i>But he always had a hearty appetite
for whatever I made him.</i>

20:00.908 --> 20:04.119
<i>Even during missions,
I was often sent to the kitchen.</i>

20:04.620 --> 20:08.332
He was such a well-behaved child,
it made me concerned.

20:09.083 --> 20:13.045
This is the first time
he's ever made a selfish request.

20:13.629 --> 20:14.713
Please, Maizuru.

20:15.673 --> 20:17.132
There's someone I want to save.

20:17.925 --> 20:19.260
Lend me your aid.

20:22.012 --> 20:23.597
I never imagined he'd become

20:23.681 --> 20:26.517
infatuated with a Northern girl
on his training journey.

20:26.600 --> 20:28.811
How do I convince him to move on?

20:29.687 --> 20:31.313
You want him to move on?

20:31.397 --> 20:35.109
I've been tasked by the lord
to care for the Young Master.

20:35.693 --> 20:37.820
I can't let my emotions
dictate my actions.

20:38.445 --> 20:41.323
Then why are you doing what you're doing?

20:41.407 --> 20:46.412
If you have preserved foods,
you don't have to bother with cooking.

20:47.663 --> 20:51.583
I know why he had an appetite
for your cooking only.

20:51.667 --> 20:54.920
I know what you put into them.

20:55.004 --> 20:55.838
Huh?

20:57.089 --> 20:58.799
It was love.

21:01.427 --> 21:02.845
What is that supposed to mean?

21:02.928 --> 21:04.680
Were you trying to be clever?

21:06.849 --> 21:10.019
But yes, I suppose
it's a little too late now.

21:10.519 --> 21:12.604
Depending on how things turn out,

21:12.688 --> 21:15.107
perhaps I can speak on his behalf.

21:15.816 --> 21:16.984
TSUGUYOSHI NAKAMOTO

21:17.067 --> 21:18.110
TOSHITSUGU NAKAMOTO

21:18.193 --> 21:19.695
NOW, TOSHIRO NAKAMOTO

21:19.778 --> 21:20.904
FALIRO NAKAMOTO

21:20.988 --> 21:22.865
It's using different art materials!

21:22.948 --> 21:25.743
I don't think that's likely just yet.

21:26.869 --> 21:28.620
Good. This will do.

21:28.704 --> 21:30.039
It's ready.

21:30.122 --> 21:32.624
AN EASTERN MEAL

21:32.708 --> 21:36.628
Now then, let us serve it while it's hot!

21:38.964 --> 21:41.508
What are you two doing here?

21:41.592 --> 21:43.469
They wanted to talk privately.

21:44.511 --> 21:46.847
Young Master, I'm coming in.

21:48.140 --> 21:49.058
Young Master!

21:50.684 --> 21:51.810
What happened?

21:53.604 --> 21:54.855
Did this man try something?

21:56.982 --> 21:58.734
Well? What happened?!

21:58.817 --> 22:01.070
Sorry. We don't know.

22:02.488 --> 22:04.031
Black magic.

22:04.114 --> 22:08.911
This man used black magic
to revive a woman using monster flesh.

22:08.994 --> 22:10.162
Black…?

22:12.414 --> 22:14.041
How could you?

22:14.625 --> 22:16.418
Do you even realize what you've done?

22:16.502 --> 22:18.962
Anyone involved with black magic,

22:19.046 --> 22:22.925
no matter their motives
or degree of magic, is a serious criminal!

22:23.008 --> 22:25.719
They're locked up
in the dark until they die,

22:25.803 --> 22:27.471
and even their corpses never return.

22:27.971 --> 22:31.767
If the elves of the west find out,
who knows what will happen to her?

22:32.559 --> 22:35.020
That is, if word
gets out from this dungeon.

22:35.896 --> 22:38.524
And I know you will
never tell anyone about this.

22:40.275 --> 22:41.151
Right?

22:46.240 --> 22:47.741
It was the only way.

22:48.742 --> 22:49.785
Please understand, Shuro.

22:52.704 --> 22:54.039
<i>Black magic?</i>

22:54.623 --> 22:57.126
<i>This is way worse than I thought.</i>

22:57.209 --> 22:58.502
<i>What's going to happen now?</i>

23:21.900 --> 23:24.027
Lord Delgal…

23:25.737 --> 23:28.073
I must find him.

25:00.165 --> 25:02.000
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
